{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-99cbed3a464e72fe", "type": "tool_result", "content": "=== 2506.22023 ===\n# Robust and Efficient Autoregressive Speech Synthesis with Dynamic Chunk-wise Prediction Policy\narXiv: 2506.22023\nAuthors: Bohan Li, Zhihan Li, Haoran Wang, Hanglei Zhang, Yiwei Guo, Hankun Wang, Xie Chen, Kai Yu\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Introduction of a dynamic chunk-wise autoregressive synthesis framework (DCAR) that utilizes a chunk-to-frame attention mechanism trained with multi-token prediction to dynamically adjust token prediction spans.\n  2. Significant reduction of sequence length dependency in autoregressive speech synthesis while maintaining high generation quality.\n  3. Achievement of up to 72.27% improvement in intelligibility and 2.61× inference speedup simultaneously compared to traditional next-token prediction models.\n  4. Development of a lightweight on-policy module (DCPO) that effectively optimizes the dynamic chunk prediction policy for variable speech contexts.\n  5. Demonstration of the method's versatility and scalability across different tokenizers, large-scale datasets, and open-source TTS frameworks like CosyVoice.\n\nTags: TTS/架构-AR-LLM, TTS/功能-RL优化, TTS/功能-快速生成\n\n=== 2509.17765 ===\n# Qwen3-Omni Technical Report\narXiv: 2509.17765\nAuthors: Jin Xu, Zhifang Guo, Hangrui Hu, Yunfei Chu, Xiong Wang, Jinzheng He, Yuxuan Wang, Xian Shi, Ting He, Xinfa Zhu, Yuanjun Lv, Yongqi Wang, Dake Guo, He Wang, Linhan Ma, Pei Zhang, Xinyu Zhang, Hongkun Hao, Zishan Guo, Baosong Yang, Bin Zhang, Ziyang Ma, Xipin Wei, Shuai Bai, Keqin Chen, Xuejing Liu, Peng Wang, Mingkun Yang, Dayiheng Liu, Xingzhang Ren, Bo Zheng, Rui Men, Fan Zhou, Bowen Yu, Jianxin Yang, Le Yu, Jingren Zhou, Junyang Lin\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: audio_understanding\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Qwen3-Omni is the first single multimodal model to maintain state-of-the-art performance across text, image, audio, and video without degradation relative to single-modal counterparts.\n  2. The model adopts a Thinker-Talker Mixture-of-Experts architecture that unifies perception and generation across text, images, audio, and video to yield fluent text and natural real-time speech.\n  3. It replaces the Whisper audio encoder with an Audio Transformer encoder trained from scratch on 20 million hours of supervised audio to yield stronger general-purpose audio representations.\n  4. A multi-codebook autoregressive scheme with a multi-token prediction module is introduced for speech generation, replacing block-wise diffusion with a lightweight causal ConvNet.\n  5. The system supports text interaction in 119 languages, speech understanding in 19 languages, and speech generation in 10 languages.\n  6. A Time-aligned Multimodal Rotary Position Embedding interleaves rotary angles across temporal, height, and width dimensions to enhance long-range dependency modeling for multimodal streams.\n  7. A Thinking model is introduced to explicitly reason over inputs from any modality, including audio-video and audio-only scenarios.\n  8. Qwen3-Omni-30B-A3B-Captioner is fine-tuned to produce detailed, low-hallucination captions for arbitrary audio inputs to address the lack of general-purpose audio captioning models.\n  9. The model achieves a theoretical end-to-end first-packet latency of 234 ms in cold-start settings through chunked prefilling and streaming multi-codebook codec generation.\n\nTags: LALM, LALM/对话型, LALM/潜在表示, LALM/对话型-并行生成, TTS, TTS/架构-AR-LLM, TTS/功能-流式\n\n=== 2606.09141 ===\n# FlashTTS: Fast Streaming TTS with MTP Acceleration and X-pred Mean Flow Distillation\narXiv: 2606.09141\nAuthors: Hanke Xie, Xiaming Ren, Dake Guo, Ruonan You, Wenhao Li, Jingbin Hu, Guobin Ma, Huakang Chen, Kejie Xu, Rui Huang, Weiguo Tan, Xianrong Wang, Lei Xie\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: \nStatus: unread\n\n=== 2601.15621 ===\n# Qwen3-TTS Technical Report\narXiv: 2601.15621\nAuthors: Hangrui Hu, Xinfa Zhu, Ting He, Dake Guo, Bin Zhang, Xiong Wang, Zhifang Guo, Ziyue Jiang, Hongkun Hao, Zishan Guo, Xinyu Zhang, Pei Zhang, Baosong Yang, Jin Xu, Jingren Zhou, Junyang Lin\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Introduction of the Qwen3-TTS series, a family of advanced multilingual, controllable, robust, and streaming text-to-speech models.\n  2. Development of Qwen-TTS-Tokenizer-25Hz, a single-codebook codec that integrates semantic and acoustic cues for seamless LLM integration and streaming waveform reconstruction.\n  3. Development of Qwen-TTS-Tokenizer-12Hz, a multi-codebook codec achieving extreme bitrate reduction and ultra-low-latency streaming with a first-packet latency as low as 97 ms.\n  4. Design of a dual-track autoregressive language model architecture incorporating a Multi-Token Prediction module for real-time streaming synthesis.\n  5. Achievement of state-of-the-art performance in zero-shot voice cloning, cross-lingual speech generation, and natural language instruction-following for voice design.\n  6. Demonstration of exceptional stability in long-form generation, capable of synthesizing over 10 minutes of fluent speech without chunk-based artifacts.\n  7. Open-sourcing of the complete family of Qwen3-TTS models and tokenizers under the Apache 2.0 license to facilitate community research.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-AR-LLM, TTS/功能-流式, TTS/功能-多语言, TTS/控制-NL描述, 压缩, 压缩/量化-RVQ\n\n=== 2602.06602 ===\n# Scaling Speech Tokenizers with Diffusion Autoencoders\narXiv: 2602.06602\nAuthors: Yuancheng Wang, Zhenyu Tang, Yun Wang, Arthur Hinsvark, Yingru Liu, Yinghao Li, Kainan Peng, Junyi Ao, Mingbo Ma, Mike Seltzer, Qing He, Xubo Liu\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: codec_vae\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We propose SiTok, a diffusion autoencoder-based speech tokenizer that jointly optimizes quantization and high-fidelity reconstruction in an end-to-end framework.\n  2. We introduce semantic regularization via an auxiliary CTC loss to explicitly enforce linguistic consistency in the discrete latent space, significantly enhancing downstream speech understanding.\n  3. We scale SiTok to 1.6B parameters trained on 2 million hours of speech, achieving strong performance at an extremely low token rate of 12.5 Hz and bitrate of 200 bits-per-second.\n  4. We apply shortcut fine-tuning and a lightweight diffusion head to drastically accelerate diffusion decoding while maintaining high reconstruction quality.\n  5. We conduct extensive ablation studies providing practical insights into the trade-offs between reconstruction objectives, codebook configurations, and frame rates for scalable speech tokenizers.\n\nTags: 压缩, 压缩/量化-RVQ, 压缩/语义声学-语义, Vocoder, Vocoder/Diffusion\n\n=== 2507.16632 ===\n# Step-Audio 2 Technical Report\narXiv: 2507.16632\nAuthors: Boyong Wu, Chao Yan, Chen Hu, Cheng Yi, Chengli Feng, Fei Tian, Feiyu Shen, Gang Yu, Haoyang Zhang, Jingbei Li, Mingrui Chen, Peng Liu, Wang You, Xiangyu Tony Zhang, Xingyuan Li, Xuerui Yang, Yayue Deng, Yechang Huang, Yuxin Li, Yuxin Zhang, Zhao You, Brian Li, Changyi Wan, Hanpeng Hu, Jiangjie Zhen, Siyu Chen, Song Yuan, Xuelin Zhang, Yimin Jiang, Yu Zhou, Yuxiang Yang, Bingxin Li, Buyun Ma, Changhe Song, Dongqing Pang, Guoqiang Hu, Haiyang Sun, Kang An, Na Wang, Shuli Gao, Wei Ji, Wen Li, Wen Sun, Xuan Wen, Yong Ren, Yuankai Ma, Yufan Lu, Bin Wang, Bo Li, Changxin Miao, Che Liu, Chen Xu, Dapeng Shi, Dingyuan Hu, Donghang Wu, Enle Liu, Guanzhe Huang, Gulin Yan, Han Zhang, Hao Nie, Haonan Jia, Hongyu Zhou, Jianjian Sun, Jiaoren Wu, Jie Wu, Jie Yang, Jin Yang, Junzhe Lin, Kaixiang Li, Lei Yang, Liying Shi, Li Zhou, Longlong Gu, Ming Li, Mingliang Li, Mingxiao Li, Nan Wu, Qi Han, Qinyuan Tan, Shaoliang Pang, Shengjie Fan, Siqi Liu, Tiancheng Cao, Wanying Lu, Wenqing He, Wuxun Xie, Xu Zhao, Xueqi Li, Yanbo Yu, Yang Yang, Yi Liu, Yifan Lu, Yilei Wang, Yuanhao Ding, Yuanwei Liang, Yuanwei Lu, Yuchu Luo, Yuhe Yin, Yumeng Zhan, Yuxiang Zhang, Zidong Yang, Zixin Zhang, Binxing Jiao, Daxin Jiang, Heung-Yeung Shum, Jiansheng Chen, Jing Li, Xiangyu Zhang, Yibo Zhu\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: audio_understanding\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Integrates discrete audio token generation into language modeling to achieve genuine end-to-end speech conversation and enhance responsiveness to paralinguistic information.\n  2. Leverages a latent audio encoder and reasoning-centric reinforcement learning to improve speech and audio understanding.\n  3. Incorporates retrieval-augmented generation and external tool calling, including a novel audio search tool for timbre and speaking style switching, to mitigate hallucination and leverage real-world knowledge.\n  4. Develops a multi-stage training strategy trained on millions of hours of diverse audio and textual data to ensure robust intelligence and expressiveness.\n  5. Introduces new evaluation benchmarks for paralinguistic understanding and tool calling to assess complex audio interaction capabilities.\n  6. Achieves state-of-the-art performance across multiple audio understanding and speech conversation benchmarks, outperforming existing open-source and commercial solutions.\n\nTags: LALM/音频标记-融合, LALM/对话型-交错标记, LALM/后训练-GRPO, LALM/训练-指令微调", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "765fd72b-b113-4d3e-811a-dee2183633bb", "uuid": "a80d2758-ad6c-4a13-a147-2542e53c66ac", "timestamp": "2026-08-03T08:30:03.368Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "=== 2506.22023 ===\n# Robust and Efficient Autoregressive Speech Synthesis with Dynamic Chunk-wise Prediction Policy\narXiv: 2506.22023\nAuthors: Bohan Li, Zhihan Li, Haoran Wang, Hanglei Zhang, Yiwei Guo, Hankun Wang, Xie Chen, Kai Yu\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Introduction of a dynamic chunk-wise autoregressive synthesis framework (DCAR) that utilizes a chunk-to-frame attention mechanism trained wi